cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PhysDDG, please cite it as below, and cite the datasets and tools listed in THIRD_PARTY.md."
title: "PhysDDG: a GPU-batched, physics-inspired predictor of protein stability changes upon mutation"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-27
license: MIT
type: software
authors:
  - name: "PhysDDG contributors"
abstract: >-
  Structure-based predictor of single-substitution folding stability changes (ddG, positive = destabilising)
  that uses force-field-style energy terms, a PDB-derived rotamer library and a small linear model; no deep
  learning. The code, data curation, benchmarks and audits were produced by AI agents (Claude, Anthropic)
  directed by an AI principal-investigator agent; see docs/PROVENANCE.md.
keywords:
  - protein stability
  - ddG
  - mutation effect prediction
  - AlphaFold
